meta {
  name: Pages
  seq: 24
}

docs {
  Workflow pages: a hosted form-and-result page in front of a workflow, so
  people can run it without opening the canvas. Every page belongs to one
  workflow. Viewing and using pages needs `page.view`; building, publishing
  and sharing them needs `page.manage`.

  ## Lifecycle

  - **Draft vs live.** `content` is the draft the builder edits
    (`Pages - Update`); `published_content` is what people see, copied from
    the draft by `Pages - Publish` — which refuses (422) while the draft has
    error-level `issues`. `Pages - Unpublish` takes it down again.
  - **Access.** `workspace` (default) pages are used from inside the app
    (`Pages - View`, `Submissions - Create`). `link` and `password` pages are
    also served at the public link — see below. Public access needs the
    plan's public-pages feature (403 otherwise).
  - **Variants (A/B).** `Variant - Create` copies the draft into a version
    B. Publishing then makes both live; visitors are bucketed by
    `variant_split` (% to B). `Variant - Promote` makes B the draft (publish
    to go live), `Variant - Remove` ends the test.
  - **Versions.** Every publish snapshots a version; `Versions - Save` adds a
    labelled one by hand, `Versions - Restore` copies one back into the
    draft (after snapshotting the current draft).
  - **Generations.** `Generations - Create` asks AI to design or rework the
    draft. It's queued (202) — poll `Generations - Get` until `status` is
    `completed` or `failed`. Costs credits.

  ## Public link

  Each page has a `public_token` (stored in `pageToken` by `Pages - Create`,
  `Pages - Get`, `Pages - Update` and `Pages - Rotate Link`). The
  `Public Page - ...` requests hit `/v1/p/{token}` with no auth. They answer
  404 unless the page is published, `is_enabled`, and `access` is `link` or
  `password`. Setting a new password or rotating the link changes the
  token and kills the old one.

  ## Variables

  `pageId`, `pageToken`, `pageGenerationId`, `pageSectionId`,
  `pageVersionId`, `pageCommentId`, `pageSubmissionId`,
  `publicPageSubmissionId`, `publicPageSubmissionSecret`,
  `pageAccessToken`. Also needs `workflowId` (any workflow with an
  interface). Page templates live in the `Templates` folder.

  ## Suggested order

  `Pages - Create` → `Pages - Update` (set `access: link`) →
  `Versions` / `Comments` / `Variant` as needed → `Pages - Publish` →
  `Pages - View` / `Submissions - Create` → `Public Page - Get` →
  `Public Page - Submit` → `Public Page - Get Submission` →
  `Insights - Get` / `Submissions - Export` → `Pages - Unpublish` →
  `Pages - Delete`.
}
